      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f5b03bf7",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: yall_wanna_see_a_stupid_post; hasOverallIntent: self-deprecating humor; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a group of people in a movie theater, reacting with exaggerated shock and awe to something on screen. The text overlay reads 'y'all wanna see a stupid post'. The overall intent is self-deprecating humor, where the creator is jokingly admitting they are about to share something they consider trivial or uninteresting, using the visual of audience members reacting dramatically to imply the post will be so bad or silly that it's worth the exaggerated reaction. There is no toxicity, harmful content, or hateful messaging present. The meme relies on the contrast between the intense audience reaction and the mundane text to create comedic effect, not to attack or demean any group or individual.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_26c87df9"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
